From f82e243a80d87ecee88da1b71cde3c206fda216e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 13:22:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 436/913] drivers: stm32_lptimer: clock enable timer in probe
 sequence of the driver

Due to a modification of the clock framework, it is not possible to
enable a clock in an interrupt context.
To fix this we enable the clock to access the registers in the probe
sequence and add a pm sequence to disable the clock before suspending.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 3fea6b6c7e6f16c8ed7eeaa275391a17beda5aee drivers: stm32_lptimer: clock enable timer in probe sequence of the driver]
Change-Id: Ida02c2a9a6ae32b4ebc42958d0376fbb09d6d20d
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/570249
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
